<p><span style="text-transform: uppercase"><span style="letter-spacing: 2.4pt"><b>199 - Know That There is Sweetening to be Saved from Punishment of Widower</b></span></span></p><p><span class="body-text">Know that there is a sweetening to be saved from the punishment of becoming a widower – that one's wife not die, G-d forbid. This is the sweetness in the Torah; through it, one is saved from this punishment. The letters&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>A</b></span><span class="body-text">L</span><span class="body-text"><b>M</b></span><span class="body-text">N (-widower) are the initials of&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>M</b></span><span class="body-text">ah&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>N</b></span><span class="body-text">imlezu&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>L</b></span><span class="body-text">echiki&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>A</b></span><span class="body-text">mratcha (Psalms 119:103: &quot;</span><span class="body-text"><b>How sweet are Your words to my palate</b></span><span class="body-text">&quot;). By feeling sweetness in the Torah, one is saved from this punishment. The verse concludes: &quot;</span><span class="body-text"><b>than honey to my mouth</b></span><span class="body-text">&quot; – this sweetness sweetens the judgment of a wife's death, G-d forbid, for &quot;honey&quot; numerically equals &quot;woman&quot; (as in the writings).</span></p><p><br/><br/></p> 
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

